# ===== Glass shake
setup TESSERA_GREETER_MOCK=1 $TESSERA_BIN --greeter --style look --look glass --demo users &
wait 2
key x
rec g-shake 1.5 key -k Return
note Field dots first, then after about 600 ms of Logging in the field shakes: offsets +12, -10, +5, 0 over about 250 ms; red border and error line; compare with QML.
key -k Escape
wait 1
key -k Escape
wait 1
# ===== Material pill
setup TESSERA_GREETER_MOCK=1 $TESSERA_BIN --greeter --style look --look material --demo users &
wait 2
shot m-closed
note Material with no input: pill CLOSED (cookie avatar + name only), clock at 18 % height.
rec m-open 1.5 ptr move 900 500 sleep 100 glide 960 560 200 sleep 800
note Pointer moved more than 2 px: pill springs open to 360 px width with placeholder "Enter password"; measure the open time against QML (spring 600 ms, damping 0.5 is a possible curve difference).
wait 11
shot m-reclosed
note About 10 s after the last input the pill is closed again.
key a
wait 0.5
shot m-key-open
note A letter key opens the pill with one dot.
# Material power
# MANUAL: click Restart once: button turns error-container, say pill "Restart: press Enter or click it again"; press and hold a Round button: corners square off (22 to 14)
# MANUAL: Material analog clock (lock.clockFace analog in the arena's greeter config): at a minute change the minute hand steps 6 degrees forward with overshoot; at :00 forward 6 degrees, not a full turn back
# Tab cycles sessions
key -k Tab
wait 0.5
shot m-tab
note Tab changed the session chip text to the next session (wraps); compare with QML.
key -k Escape
wait 1
key -k Escape
wait 1
setup TESSERA_GREETER_MOCK=1 $TESSERA_BIN --greeter --style look --look glass --demo users &
wait 2
key -k Tab
wait 0.5
shot g-tab
note Tab cycled the session "Name  ▾" under the field to the next one (wraps).
key -k Down
wait 0.5
shot g-down
note Down chose the next person (name changes, field empty).
key -k Escape
wait 1
